WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.910
- So former officer Derek
Chauvin was convicted

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.290
and he was convicted on
three different counts.

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:06.580
And I've gotten so many questions

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.050
about how can a criminal
defendant be convicted

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.260
of three different crimes
based on the same conduct.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:13.410
- [Judge] Find the defendant guilty.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.660
- Here Chauvin was convicted
of second degree murder,

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.930
which in Minnesota is the
felony murder statute.

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:19.490
Then you have murder in the third degree.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:21.700
And finally, second degree manslaughter.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.690
Chauvin will not serve
jail related to all three.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.760
The constitution prohibits
double punishment

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.620
for the same crime.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:28.881
Chauvin will only serve time

00:00:28.881 --> 00:00:30.740
related to the most serious offense

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.570
because that's the one that
carries the most jail time.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:35.153
So now you know next
time I see you in court.

